{"diagnosis": "TRAP reports uart data mismatch got 0x00 want 0xa5 on loopback send 0xa5. Excerpt line 53 returns recv_buf_data when recv_buf_valid, but reset lines 71-72 init recv_buf_data<=0 with recv_buf_valid<=1, so the first read spuriously returns 0x00. Root cause is reset value of recv_buf_valid should be 0 (empty), not 1 (cone: picosoc/simpleuart.v:20, picosoc/picosoc.v:124, picosoc/picosoc.v:204).", "patch_diff": "diff --git a/picosoc/simpleuart.v b/picosoc/simpleuart.v
--- a/picosoc/simpleuart.v
+++ b/picosoc/simpleuart.v
@@ -66,7 +66,7 @@
 		if (!resetn) begin
 			recv_state <= 0;
 			recv_divcnt <= 0;
 			recv_pattern <= 0;
 			recv_buf_data <= 0;
-			recv_buf_valid <= 1;
+			recv_buf_valid <= 0;
 		end else begin
", "expected": "tohost PASS (no TRAP: uart data mismatch, loopback got 0xa5 want 0xa5)"}

